-- What's new: the latest versions' notes for the settings panel.
-- GENERATED by tools/changelog2lua.js from CHANGELOG.md; do not edit by hand.
local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.0.4", text = "A big batch from your ideas: names above the nameplates, Blizzard's cast bar glow, stacked buffs and debuffs, and item levels in the inspect window. It also brings smoother nameplates in big pulls and the normal game font back.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r the game font is back to normal. 7.0.3 swapped it for Blizzard's Russian copy by accident, which looked sharper and drew some symbols as boxes. Liked the sharper look? Pick |cffffffffFriz Quadrata TT (Crisp)|r in any font list.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r Name Only plates show players' full names. Switch |cffffffffShow Full Name|r off for first names only.\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffName Above Plates|r is now called |cffffffffName Above Frames|r.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r names above the plate, and smoother plates in big pulls.\n• |cffffffffCast bars:|r Blizzard's bright edge at the front of the cast.\n• |cffffffffBuffs and Debuffs|r can share a place on the unit, party and boss frames.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffNames Above Plate|r (Off) on the Style tab: the name above the plate, left, centre or right, first or full name. Buffs and debuffs move up to make room.\n• |cffffffffShow Full Name|r (on) in the Name Only Mode section.\n• |cffffffffEdge Glow|r on the Cast Bar tab.\n\n|cffe6cc99Cast Bars|r\n• |cffffffffEdge Glow|r: a bright edge at the front of the cast, as on Blizzard's cast bars.\n      - In each frame's Cast Bar section in Edit Mode, and under Look on the Player Cast Bar.\n      - On for new players. Already using FlareUI? Switch it on there.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffBuffs|r and |cffffffffDebuffs|r can pick the same place, or the same edge: they stack. The one placed first stays next to the frame, the other goes one row further out. Party and boss frames too.\n• |cffffffffRange Check|r (off) on Target of Target and Target of Focus.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• |cffffffffShow in Caster Form|r (off) on the Druid Mana bar: it stays up in caster form too.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags|r\n• |cffffffffReverse Bag Fill|r (off): the backpack starts at the top left and fills left to right, downwards.\n• |cffffffffItem Level|r also shows on the inspect window's slots, with the player's average item level under their name.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffBelow the Map|r (off) in the Info Bar section: the bar sits under the minimap, clear of the quest arrow.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• |cffffffffHide Until Next Group|r in the meter's gear menu: the meter goes away until you join another group, or reload.\n\n|cffe6cc99Fonts|r\n• |cffffffffFriz Quadrata TT (Crisp)|r: Blizzard's sharper copy of the game font. It lacks a few symbols.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the Visibility tab works with the Nameplates module off. Those are Blizzard's own nameplate settings, so you can switch In Combat back off.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the settings preview shows aura timers and swipes.\n• |cffffffffAction Bars:|r |cffffffffUpdate Spell Ranks|r moves your pet's spells up too (a warlock's Torment after the grimoire).\n• |cffffffffBuffs & Debuffs:|r |cffffffffFiltered Auras|r marks debuffs the game won't let addons hide on you as |cffffffffNot on You|r.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menu:|r a |cffffd100/click FUIRadial|r macro opens the radial for the controller while the Gamepad UI is on.\n• |cffffffffAbout:|r Kabaday is credited for the loot roll window and the Cooldown Manager.\n• |cffffffffFrench:|r the 7.0.2 and 7.0.3 text is translated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r with Blizzard's Gamepad UI on, a mouse click on a quest showed \"Open your quest log\" instead of opening it.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r quests that Blizzard's own tracker doesn't list open on a click too.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r less stutter in big pulls. Out of Range Opacity, threat colours and glows do far less work per mob.\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r tooltips showed boxes instead of the \"·\" dot." },
    { version = "7.0.3", text = "More nameplate polish, plus fixes for the bugs you sent in after 7.0.2. Nameplate auras get their own look options and can stack in two lines.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r player names on full plates are white. Class colour stays on Name Only plates, where it is easy to read.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r no longer sits over the name. It shows in the level box instead of the level while you have threat. With |cffffffffLevel|r off, it gets its own small box right of the plate, shown only in a fight.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the raid marker sits on the side opposite the quest icon. |cffffffffDefensives|r and |cffffffffCrowd Control|r go past it on its side.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffAuras|r section at the top of the Auras tab, for each plate type:\n      - |cffffffffAura Icon Shape|r (Square)\n      - |cffffffffAura Swipe|r, |cffffffffAura Timer|r and |cffffffffTimer Colour|r: start with your Unit Frames values, so nothing changes.\n• |cffffffffAura Positions|r section below Debuffs, shown when both Buffs and Debuffs are on:\n      - |cffffffffPosition|r (One Line): |cffffffffOne Line|r keeps them side by side, as before.\n      - |cffffffffBuffs on Top|r or |cffffffffDebuffs on Top|r: each gets its own line across the whole plate, one line at most.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffQuest Objective|r and |cffffffffQuest Progress|r no longer show for the two player plate types.\n• |cffffffffFrench:|r the 7.0.1 text is translated. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffChat:|r with |cffffffffFade Old Lines|r on, names are clickable again and link tooltips no longer flicker.\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames:|r |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r works on the player frame again. Other frames no longer need one hover after Edit Mode.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting:|r a switched-off module stays off after a reload.\n• |cffffffffFonts:|r Russian names show in the meter on English clients. FlareUI uses Blizzard's Cyrillic fonts where the game has them. Fix from Aleksandr Vasinskyi.\n• |cffffffffBuffs & Debuffs:|r the |cffffffffPick One of Yours|r list no longer errors in a fight." },
    { version = "7.0.2", text = "A quick hotfix for four things 7.0.1 broke or missed. Thanks for reporting them so fast.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r a left click on a quest opens it again. 7.0.1 only showed \"Open your quest log to read this quest\" for most quests.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r the crafting bag shows its items in the combined backpack again (|cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack|r). 7.0.1 left the section empty when you opened only the backpack.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r |cffffffffFull Name|r is a choice in the plate's |cffffffffHealth Text|r, so friendly players can show their surname. 7.0.1 drew it but left it out of the list.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r the raid marker sits right beside full plates. The |cffffffffDefensives|r icons now go past it instead of pushing it far to the left." },
    { version = "7.0.1", text = "Sorry, everyone. The new nameplates came with more bugs than they should have, and the fixes took longer than I wanted. This update fixes every nameplate bug you reported, plus a long list of other fixes. Thank you for your patience and for all the reports.\n\nA big thank you to this release's contributors: |cffffffffalex47|r (the Items section, Healing & Damage, the preview fix), |cffffffffparchinskiy|r (collapsible backpack sections), |cffffffffBraincell1980|r (the French translation) and |cffffffffArchy|r (the complete Russian translation).\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r the right-click menu no longer has |cffffffffOpen Quest Log|r or |cffffffffShow on Map|r. A left click on a quest opens both.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r |cffffffffBorder|r now only borders the chat window. The edit box has its own border option and keeps the look it had.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r the Combat Log tab can be moved like any other tab. General stays first.\n• |cffffffffTooltips:|r |cffffffffShow Item Level|r, |cffffffffCompare with Shift|r and |cffffffffSimplified Item Stats|r moved to a new |cffffffffItems|r section on the Content tab.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r every bug you reported is fixed, including the stutter when combat starts and ends.\n• |cffffffffBags:|r collapsible backpack sections, and filling crates from the crafting bag works again.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r NPC titles like \"General Goods\" under Name Only names.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• NPC titles under the name on Name Only plates, in a soft tan. Always on.\n• |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r now shows during fights.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags|r\n• Click a section header in |cffffffffCategory Rows|r and |cffffffffCategory Rows + Sets|r to collapse or expand it. By parchinskiy.\n      - Each character remembers its own sections.\n\n|cffe6cc99Tooltips|r\n• |cffffffffItems|r section on the Content tab. By alex47.\n• |cffffffffHealing & Damage|r (Off): shortens item lines with both healing and damage. By alex47.\n      - |cffffffffSpell Healing / Spell Damage:|r both numbers as they are.\n      - |cffffffffSpell Healing / Spell Power:|r the damage as Spell Power, plus the extra healing.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffEdit Box Style|r (Modern):\n      - |cffffffffFlareUI:|r Blizzard's own edit box, in FlareUI's bronze.\n      - |cffffffffModern:|r a dark box.\n• |cffffffffEdit Box Border|r (follows your old chat border): |cffffffffNone|r, |cffffffffFlareUI Thick|r or |cffffffffFlareUI Thin|r. Shows with Modern only.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• |cffffffffPaladin Seals:|r |cffffffffShow Icon|r (off) in Edit Mode puts the seal's icon at the bar's left end.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• |cffffffffWarlock pet:|r right-click the icon to pick the demon a click summons: |cffffffffLast Used|r (default) or any demon you know.\n• Every icon's right-click menu has a |cffffffffFlareUI Settings|r link.\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• The |cffffffffVoice Button|r also plays quest lines from Wayfarer (Russian voice-over).\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffInfo Bar:|r gold shows with coin icons, like in your bags.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffUnit Frames (Forever Style):|r your own name box takes your class colour when that frame's |cffffffffClass Colours|r is on, as on target and party.\n• |cffffffffLanguages:|r\n      - Russian: complete (739 new strings). By Archy.\n      - French: 7.0 strings translated. By Braincell1980.\n• |cffffffffRussian client:|r a dash replaces the middle dot \"·\", which Russian fonts draw as a box.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• A stutter when combat started and ended.\n• |cffffffffShow Friendly Plates|r reset to Off when you picked |cffffffffAlways|r. |cffffffffIn Combat|r and Quality of Life's |cffffffffCombat Friendly Plates|r didn't work either.\n• Chairs, signs, mailboxes and herb or ore nodes got enemy plates.\n• Pet and minor names were tiny, even at 200%.\n• |cffffffffFull Name|r in Bar Text showed only the first name.\n• The raid marker sat far from the name on Name Only plates.\n• Friendly players showed two names with the Musician addon.\n• Quest marks stayed beside plates when another nameplate addon was running, and couldn't be turned off.\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags|r\n• Filling a crate, milling or prospecting from the crafting bag was blocked (|cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack|r).\n\n|cffe6cc99Quest Tracker|r\n• After you opened a quest from the tracker, the world map could be blocked in a fight.\n\n|cffe6cc99Gamepad|r\n• A \"blocked action\" popup after closing Edit Mode. In Gamepad mode, Edit Mode dropdowns and colour swatches now open FlareUI's own lists. Colour swatches offer ready colours.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• The chat tabs took clicks meant for quest, merchant and crafting windows above them.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• |cffffffffXP Bar:|r a small gap stayed at the bottom of the screen.\n• |cffffffffSettings previews:|r squeezed previews cut their text short. By alex47." },
    { version = "7.0", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nFlareUI now draws its own nameplates. Every kind of unit gets its own look: enemy players and NPCs, friendly players and NPCs, and minor mobs with pets and totems. Open-world PvP gets full plates, quest givers get a clean name, and you can tweak every one of them with a live preview at your side. The chat also learned a few tricks, and unit frames can show the name above the frame.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things look or work differently even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffChat:|r a popped-out chat window now fades on its own. It comes back for its own messages only, not for every line in every window.\n• |cffffffffVisibility Never:|r a frame set to Never no longer shows tooltips when you point where it is.\n• |cffffffffRadial Menus:|r the |cffffffffMounts|r catalog is now |cffffffffCollections|r, with your mounts and your toys.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r FlareUI's own nameplates, with a setup for each unit type.\n• |cffffffffName Above Plates:|r the name above any unit frame, so the bars stay clean.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r fade old lines one by one, and quiet loot and skill-ups.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates (new page, off)|r\n• First in the Combat list. A /reload turns it on or off.\n• |cffffffffUnit types|r, each with its own setup: |cffffffffEnemy Player|r, |cffffffffEnemy NPC|r, |cffffffffFriendly Player|r, |cffffffffFriendly NPC|r and |cffffffffMinor|r (minor mobs, pets, totems and guardians).\n• |cffffffffPresets|r for each unit: |cffffffffFull|r, |cffffffffSimple|r, |cffffffffMinimal|r, |cffffffffName Only|r. Change any setting and it becomes that unit's own Custom.\n      - Friendly players and NPCs start on Name Only.\n• |cffffffffLive Preview|r beside the settings, and |cffffffffTest in Game|r to put the look on the plates around you.\n• |cffffffffPlate:|r size, |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r, |cffffffffBar Texture|r, |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffLevel|r, |cffffffffBar Effects|r, |cffffffffColour By|r, |cffffffffHealth Text|r.\n      - |cffffffffName Only Mode|r: just the name, with |cffffffffName Only Size|r.\n      - |cffffffffShow Plates in Combat|r: picked units leave Name Only in a fight.\n• |cffffffffExtras:|r\n      - Icons: |cffffffffElite & Rare|r, |cffffffffCombo Points|r, |cffffffffQuest Objective|r, |cffffffffQuest Progress|r.\n      - Threat: |cffffffffColour by Threat|r, |cffffffffRole|r, |cffffffffThreat Glow|r, |cffffffffAggro Flash|r, |cffffffffThreat Scale|r, |cffffffffThreat Percentage|r.\n      - Colours: |cffffffffExecute Range|r, |cffffffffColour Mob Types|r, |cffffffffParty Colour|r, |cffffffffRaid Colour|r.\n• |cffffffffCast Bar:|r icon, timer and target, |cffffffffKick Ready Colour|r, |cffffffffKick Ready Mark|r, |cffffffffFlash When Targeted|r, |cffffffffHighlight Important Casts|r.\n• |cffffffffAuras:|r buffs, debuffs, |cffffffffDefensives|r and |cffffffffCrowd Control|r, each with size and count.\n• |cffffffffTargeting|r (all plates): target and non-target scale and opacity, |cffffffffOut of Range|r and |cffffffffOut of Sight|r fading, target |cffffffffArrow|r, |cffffffffBorder|r, |cffffffffBar Colour|r, |cffffffffOuter Glow|r and |cffffffffFocus Colour|r.\n• |cffffffffVisibility|r (all plates):\n      - Which enemies and friends get a plate, |cffffffffStacking|r, |cffffffffKeep Target on Screen|r, |cffffffffClick-Through|r.\n      - |cffffffffName Only While Unattackable|r (off): enemy NPCs you can't attack yet show only their name.\n      - The game's names over heads: |cffffffffNPC Names|r, |cffffffffPlayer Names|r, |cffffffffMinion Names|r.\n• |cffffffffNameplate Colours|r in FlareUI's colour window, and a Fonts tab.\n• |cffffd100/fui plates|r prints what the module sees, for bug reports.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffName Above Plates|r (Off), in the Text section in Edit Mode: First Name or Full Name above the frame, on the left, centre or right.\n      - Auras and a cast bar above the frame move up to make room.\n      - On the player, target, focus, pet, target of target, target of focus, party, boss and flag carrier frames. Not on Forever Style, which has its name box.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffOnly Chat Messages|r: a new Visibility choice. Only lines people write bring the chat back; loot, skill-ups and XP stay quiet.\n• |cffffffffFade Old Lines|r (off), under Fading in Edit Mode: lines fade one by one, oldest first. Pointing at the chat or typing brings them back.\n\n|cffe6cc99Visibility|r\n• |cffffffffNot in a Capital City|r: last on every Visibility list, the reverse of In a Capital City.\n• |cffffffffFade Delay|r goes up to 1 minute (chat and meter).\n\n|cffe6cc99Radial Menus|r\n• |cffffffffCollections|r catalog: mounts, then toys.\n• Small titles split the catalog's lists: Mounts and Toys, Spells and Pet Spells, Target and World Markers, General and Character Macros, Professions and Profession Spells.\n\n|cffe6cc99Other|r\n• |cffffffffXP Bar:|r |cffffffffShow Tooltip|r (off) brings the bar's tooltip back.\n• |cffffd100/fui buff|r opens the Buff Reminders settings.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Settings text: clearer descriptions and tips, using the options' real names.\n• Faster in several places: nameplate colours, buff reminder aura checks, resource bar text and the heal bars on party frames.\n• French: the 6.14 phrases. By Brainc3ll.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Chat: the mouse wheel scrolls the chat again, also when the game's own chat scroll setting is off." },
}
